  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. Here KKK is fixed to be 333.**\n\nYou are given 222 integers, NNN and K(K=3)K (K = 3)K(K=3).\n\nCount the number of permutations PPP of the integers [1,N][1, N][1,N] satisfying the following condition:\n\n\n(Pi+Pi+1)mod  K≠0(P_i + P_{i + 1}) \\mod K \\ne 0(Pi​+Pi+1​)modK=0 for all 1≤i&lt;N1 \\le i &lt; N1≤i&lt;N\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of valid permutations modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "K=3K = 3K=3",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6\n2 3\n3 3\n4 3\n6 3\n10 3\n190000 3",
        "output": "0\n2\n4\n80\n72576\n252292730",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : There are no valid permutations. The 222 possible permutations [1,2][1, 2][1,2] and [2,1][2, 1][2,1], both have (P1+P2)mod  3=0(P_1 + P_2) \\mod 3 = 0(P1​+P2​)mod3=0.\nTest Case 2 : The 222 valid permutations are [1,3,2][1, 3, 2][1,3,2] and [2,3,1][2, 3, 1][2,3,1]."
      }
    ]
